  {
    "episode_id": 95367,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95367.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "Tough to tell. I hope that my former colleagues and I believe that many of them privately will agree with everything we're seeing in this brief. Because again, this is just all about establishing that Trump did commit insurrection against the Constitution, we as former members want to make sure it never happens again. Each and every one of my former colleagues, the members who are still there taking oath, just like I did, to defend in uphold the Constitution. That's a big part of what this is all about. And I would hope they understand and they agree with us that we don't Congress was a target of violence on January 6. We don't want that to happen again. I understand the politics of the moment. And I, Jennifer, I've lived with this because for the past five to six years, as I've been out there publicly against Trump as a conservative, and you've heard this, but I've had plenty of my former colleagues tell me privately, Joe, I agree with everything you say about him. But I get that they can't say those things publicly because to say that publicly, like my former friend and colleague Adam Kinzinger from Illinois, who's gone through the same thing I've gone through to publicly as a Republican stand up against Trump in the public square, is to pretty much end your careers a Republican. So I get the risk.",
