  {
    "episode_id": 95367,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95367.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "Yes. Well, I think it's a cascading, it could be a cascading event in a couple of areas, Jennifer, you identified one because Donald Trump, and he's on the ballot running for president again, but Donald Trump wasn't the only one who engaged in insurrection. So I think there's no doubt that this could point toward other members, other elected Republicans who did as well. I also think that this could lead to a cascading event when it comes to other states. I think no matter where you stand on this issue of, you know, the 14th Amendment Section 3, he shouldn't be on the ballot. States are looking for clarity and looking for some direction from the highest court in the land. So, you know, if the Supreme Court were to side with Colorado, that could open up other states because I know a number of states are just are waiting to get some direction.",
